Jokes aside: When you download the source from the official Nethack
site, you should end up with a single file called 'nethack-343-
src.tgz', about 3.33 MB in size. This is an archive file, like .zip
or .rar. On Windows, WinRAR can open it just fine. On Unix-like
systems, 'gunzip' should do the trick, but you might need some
configuration option to make it expand all the way: a .tgz is really
a .gz (gnu ZIP) of a .tar ("tape archive"; basically, all the files
concatenated together into one, with a tiny bit of formatting
information to mark the file boundaries and names).

Once you have the file unpacked, there should be several
subfolders ... most prominently, README, which is a plain text file
that should explain what to do next.

